{"id":"I01","text":"Hi! Let's count prime numbers.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I01.wav","duration_s":1.7335416666666668,"sha256":"552c66a9749ab639cdd78d470c5dbea7ea520afea99ec20089f5627eabd18b40","trim":{"raw_duration_s":2.45,"leading_s":0.28854166666666664,"trailing_s":0.42791666666666667,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I02","text":"A prime number is a whole number greater than one with exactly two positive factors: one and itself.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I02.wav","duration_s":6.050791666666667,"sha256":"29dd81f6b0572004f3c9de74c7e205f92503b7f8ac812d3c2076f69918ac05d5","trim":{"raw_duration_s":6.775,"leading_s":0.29120833333333335,"trailing_s":0.433,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I03","text":"A factor divides a number evenly, with nothing left over.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I03.wav","duration_s":3.453375,"sha256":"110e9db09bf84ff3ee7d5c618a0ddf496013e12e9b66399d00900bf759357435","trim":{"raw_duration_s":4.225,"leading_s":0.29204166666666664,"trailing_s":0.4795833333333333,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I04","text":"Let's try five tiles.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I04.wav","duration_s":1.4194583333333333,"sha256":"50613c1e760f6cd7d5d7f975429e90dec54e66f7684d7bb8b983cda80f9c6a0e","trim":{"raw_duration_s":2.125,"leading_s":0.2946666666666667,"trailing_s":0.410875,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I05","text":"Five makes one row of five. Its only factors are one and five.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I05.wav","duration_s":4.0084583333333335,"sha256":"8c91007b251316cd6eaa91394db98514848068e8f29fb04168f14f37e8efc399","trim":{"raw_duration_s":4.725,"leading_s":0.27466666666666667,"trailing_s":0.441875,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I06","text":"Six also makes two rows of three. Six has more than two factors, so it is not prime.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I06.wav","duration_s":5.405666666666667,"sha256":"5bc1e3ce4fd6a2579e247ff3af06f27326279899f891a88b730f8aeec062420e","trim":{"raw_duration_s":6.15,"leading_s":0.2846666666666667,"trailing_s":0.45966666666666667,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I07","text":"Turning a rectangle around does not give us new factors.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I07.wav","duration_s":3.2474583333333333,"sha256":"2152da6eb3d39ea04e62bbc4f6c9a9fafecd13c3516bd41a7915c7effbf23b64","trim":{"raw_duration_s":3.975,"leading_s":0.29704166666666665,"trailing_s":0.4305,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I08","text":"One has only one factor: one. So one is not prime.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I08.wav","duration_s":3.3004166666666666,"sha256":"a6d2920fa8730f20567c52afed62c4843b858feafa5ce6af3c0b9cd8b469151e","trim":{"raw_duration_s":4.05,"leading_s":0.2969583333333333,"trailing_s":0.452625,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"I09","text":"Now let's count every prime number below one thousand.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/I09.wav","duration_s":2.986458333333333,"sha256":"0b210bd3c04ad8ad53903d7d357f7face982377ed93f1448bb112c30882d8371","trim":{"raw_duration_s":3.775,"leading_s":0.32233333333333336,"trailing_s":0.46620833333333334,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"T002a","text":"Two has exactly two factors: one and two.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/T002a.wav","duration_s":2.49275,"sha256":"ea0ba3afb3286fddcf333199529e51d8e20a4c0e0eca8d316488e2a771c62df4","trim":{"raw_duration_s":3.25,"leading_s":0.3055833333333333,"trailing_s":0.45166666666666666,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"T002b","text":"Any larger even number has two as another factor.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/T002b.wav","duration_s":2.86725,"sha256":"17a97782de369cb3dddf3cb05cc964ff936c59771772d8913002dab7fc93feaf","trim":{"raw_duration_s":3.7,"leading_s":0.3343333333333333,"trailing_s":0.4984166666666667,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"T002c","text":"Two is the only even prime.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/T002c.wav","duration_s":1.6614166666666668,"sha256":"bf9d989a1cb3a1f481050eb85324b4b25e71c45ad50770048873472764fe7235","trim":{"raw_duration_s":2.4,"leading_s":0.29654166666666665,"trailing_s":0.44204166666666667,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"T009a","text":"Nine is odd, but three rows of three make nine.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/T009a.wav","duration_s":2.8619166666666667,"sha256":"a3fd146f95286081a9130cbed42112453684c56c02a22708f90291e26662d030","trim":{"raw_duration_s":3.625,"leading_s":0.3085,"trailing_s":0.45458333333333334,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
{"id":"T009b","text":"Nine has factors other than one and itself. It is not prime.","path":"/Users/support/codex/youtube/output/prime-counting-001-v001/speech/candidates-v001/T009b.wav","duration_s":3.5889166666666665,"sha256":"f82d2d084d41545f8844b1c78328c85dad56c96e51f214f12611e850279d6b10","trim":{"raw_duration_s":4.375,"leading_s":0.31054166666666666,"trailing_s":0.47554166666666664,"peak_normalization_gain":1},"generation":{"provider":"local-kokoro","model_id":"onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX","voice_id":"af_heart","speed":0.98,"dtype":"fp32","status":"unreviewed-candidate"}}
